      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "give me Hindi stories",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "===================================================\nSTEP 1 — GIVE 10 TRENDING STORY TOPIC IDEAS\n==================================================\nWhenever the user starts a conversation, regardless of whether they say\n\"hi\", give 10 emotionally engaging and potentially viral story topic ideas\nmatching the channel niche.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- If the user has already provided a specific story idea, DO NOT replace it\n  with unrelated topics.\n- Instead, create 10 different variations, angles, twists, or approaches based\n  on the user's idea.\n- Include a variety of family drama, village/city stories, social-message\n  stories, motivational stories, emotional twists, and relatable situations.\n- Include at least 1–2 ideas connected to current seasons, festivals,\n  celebrations, or trending social themes when appropriate.\n- Titles should be highly clickable and curiosity-driven but should still\n  match the emotional storytelling niche.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT — CRITICAL:\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array. Do NOT include any greeting, explanation,\nmarkdown formatting, backticks, or extra text before or after the JSON.\nThe response must start with [ and end with ].\n\nEach object in the array must follow this exact structure:\n[\n  {\n    \"number\": 1,\n    \"title\": \"Topic Title in Hindi\",\n    \"description\": \"One-line hook clearly showing the emotion, conflict, or twist, in Hindi\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"number\": 2,\n    \"title\": \"...\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  }\n]\n\nDo NOT add the \"Inme se konsa topic pasand aaya?\" question inside the JSON.\nInstead, after the JSON array is generated, wait silently for the user's\nnext message (they will reply with a number or a new topic).\n\nSTOP HERE.\nDo NOT ask about video duration yet.\nDo NOT write the story yet.\nWait for the user's response."
        }
      },
